[LESSON]: Verification insights and user clarification patterns
- Alloy set semantics ensure uniqueness; explicit duplicate-checking is unnecessary unless modeling selections with positional slots or tuples.
- When subset signatures are used (e.g., sig Administrator in User), scope directives (e.g., 3 Administrator) have no effect. Use facts or predicates to constrain cardinality as needed.
- Requirements referencing the number of administrators should acknowledge that, unless otherwise constrained, the total number of administrators can vary depending on the scenario and model scope.
- Role mutual exclusivity suspension during Emergency mode must clearly apply to all users as per user feedback.
- Only delegations assigned during Emergency mode are auto-revoked at its conclusion; others remain subject to standard rules.
- System liveness is satisfied by the requirement that the system must eventually return to Normal mode after Emergency, without mandating a stronger fairness property.

[EVENT]: Problem-solution pairs capturing verification insights
- [EVENT]: Syntax error in Alloy due to improper placement of 'and' after quantified formulas → Diagnosis: Alloy expects block formulas or parenthesized clauses → Solution: Wrap each quantified clause or use a single block structure.
- [EVENT]: Attempt to enforce administrator uniqueness by duplicate detection in Alloy sets → Diagnosis: Alloy sets are inherently unique; duplicates are not possible → Solution: Remove duplicate-check logic and clarify set-based uniqueness in requirements.
- [EVENT]: Subset signature scoping confusion for Administrator → Diagnosis: Alloy ignores 'n Administrator' in run scopes for subset sigs → Solution: Remove such scopes; constrain cardinality with facts or predicates as needed.
- [EVENT]: Unclear application of mutual exclusion suspension during Emergency → Diagnosis: User feedback clarified it must apply to all users → Solution: Strengthen requirement text accordingly.
- [EVENT]: Unclear post-Emergency credential update scope → Diagnosis: User clarification: only emAdmins must update → Solution: Narrow requirement to only these two.
