[LESSON]: Verification insights and user clarification patterns
- Alloy set semantics ensure uniqueness; explicit duplicate-checking is unnecessary unless modeling selections with positional slots or tuples.
- When subset signatures are used (e.g., sig Administrator in User), scope directives (e.g., 3 Administrator) have no effect. Use facts or predicates to constrain cardinality as needed.
- Requirements referencing the number of administrators should acknowledge that, unless otherwise constrained, the total number of administrators can vary depending on the scenario and model scope.
- Role mutual exclusivity suspension during Emergency mode must clearly apply to all users as per user feedback.
- Only delegations assigned during Emergency mode are auto-revoked at its conclusion; others remain subject to standard rules.
- System liveness is satisfied by the requirement that the system must eventually return to Normal mode after Emergency, without mandating a stronger fairness property.

