- Can't use sum over Boolean in Alloy → Only sum integer-valued expressions  
- Can't use top-level 'and' between quantified formulas → Wrap each implication or use block structure  
- Alloy sets are always unique; explicit duplicate checks for set fields are unnecessary  

- Fixed DelegationClearance: replaced > and >= with ClearanceOrd/lt and ClearanceOrd/lte for clearance comparisons  
- Wrapped each quantified implication/fact in parentheses to avoid syntax errors from top-level 'and'  
- All run/check scopes refer only to root/top-level signatures, never subset sigs  
- Scenario-specific administrator cardinality constraints placed in predicates, not facts  
- Delegation clearance now models "delegator must be strictly higher than delegatee" and "delegatee meets role.minClearance" using ordering predicates

